<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-04--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch14-04: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.75";
    dc:description "Universal ancestry has explicit comparative-genomic predictions and massive public datasets. Exact singularity at life's origin remains inferential, but alternatives can be meaningfully discriminated with existing data.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Test universal common ancestry against multiple-origin models using conserved molecular machinery, near-universal genes, the genetic code and rare shared features while accounting for horizontal transfer. Strong likelihood or model-selection support for one connected ancestry supports the claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "All organisms that ever lived cannot be sampled directly.", "The earliest signal is obscured by horizontal gene transfer and sequence saturation.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.86"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-04--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-04--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-04--gpt--dataset-3>;
